NUM-38: limit permeable pavement drain flow when pavement and soil are full

In LIDSolver::pavementFluxRates(), the branch for "soil and pavement layers are full"
(storage layer not full) limited storage exfiltration by the water available
but left the underdrain at the raw drain-equation rate. With a drain faster
than the soil, the drain removed more than the storage layer held, the
solver clamped the storage depth at 0, and the difference was created.
Apply the same limit (volume above the drain offset, less exfiltration and
evaporation) that the "no adjoining layers are full" branch uses.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-38_swmm600.patch

